About the Role&nbsp;&nbsp;

If you're bursting with creative ideas and love playing with the latest design tools, this could be your dream gig.&nbsp;

We're looking for an enthusiastic Art Intern to join our dynamic team! As an Art Intern, you'll get to dive headfirst into the exciting world of Advertising and Social helping us whip up eye-catching visuals for all sorts of cool clients. It’s a fantastic chance to get real-world experience build up your portfolio, and learn a ton from some truly talented folks.&nbsp;

So, what will you actually do ? Well, you'll be a key player in bringing ideas to life! You'll team up with us to figure out what our clients need, then use your skills with digital platforms and trends to cook up fresh, innovative visual stories. Think of it as translating cool social ideas into visuals that really pop! You'll get to brainstorm and create all sorts of art - from snazzy digital ads and social media graphics to website visuals and print stuff. Plus, we'll count on you to be our resident trend-spotter, keeping us in the loop on all things pop culture and design.

Now, about what makes you awesome: We'd love to see folks with a background in creative fields like Digital Design, Graphic Design, Branding, or even Experiential Activation. You are a whiz with Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator, and InDesign, and it'd be super cool if you know your way around After Effects for motion graphics, animation, or video editing. Beyond the tech stuff, we're looking for someone who loves to collaborate, communicates well, and can juggle tasks like a pro to hit those deadlines. If that sounds like you, we can't wait to meet you!

How We’ll Support You &nbsp;

Ogilvy celebrates its people. Fully. Enthusiastically. Unhesitatingly. We’ll empower you with the tools you’ll need to succeed. We’ll give you the autonomy to seek out new paths and better ways of doing things. We’ll support you with colleagues who are experts in their disciplines, drawn from across the Ogilvy network. And we’ll provide opportunities for you to do work of which you’ll be proud, with people you’ll be proud to call your teammates.&nbsp; &nbsp;

